{"nodes": [{"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_broker_live_integration_suites", "label": "Broker live-integration suites", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unit suites cover the broker adapters against hand-rolled fakes - right for fast feedback, blind to protocol corners, auth/connection bring-up and operational shape. Each suite brings the real broker up in Docker and runs scenarios against the live socket; same pattern as the #313 cluster setup, one container per suite instead of a 5-node mesh."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_protocol_level_corners", "label": "Protocol-level corners", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Quoting, escaping and header serialisation where the project's spec-reading and what the real broker accepts diverge - a fake agrees with the code by construction."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_auth_connection_bring_up", "label": "Auth / connection bring-up", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Credential format, TLS and lazy reconnect after a transient drop are never exercised by an in-process fake."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_operational_shape", "label": "Operational shape", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Broker config the code assumed exists but is not on by default - Mosquitto's allow_anonymous, RabbitMQ's definitions.json import."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_broker_test_manifest", "label": "tests/integration/brokers/package.json", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runner images install from a dedicated manifest declaring every adapter peer-dep plus fastify/ts-pattern as plain dependencies - the shape an end user has after bun add actor-ts + bun add @aws-sdk/client-s3. A fresh manifest with no peerDependencies block side-steps two bun traps that fire only inside this repo. Failure mode is loud: the first import of a missing package throws Cannot find module before any scenario starts."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_bun_install_production_trap", "label": "bun install --production skips optional peer-deps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_bun_add_optional_peer_noop_trap", "label": "bun add no-ops on an already-declared optional peer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "bun treats a package already listed in peerDependencies with optional true as declared and silently does nothing."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_optional_peer_declarations_test", "label": "OptionalPeerDeclarations.test.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The loud import failure only covers peers that have a suite here; a driver with no suite directory is declared in no manifest at all and nothing says so. This test is the quiet half: every optional peer must be declared either in this manifest or in root devDependencies, so the gap is a failing test rather than a discovery years later (#676)."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_suite_directory_layout", "label": "Three-file suite directory layout", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every suite has docker-compose.<name>.yml, Dockerfile.runner and Runner.ts; three also carry a config file their image needs (mqtt/mosquitto.conf, amqp/rabbitmq.conf, grpc/echo.proto)."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_own_scenarios_shape", "label": "Own-scenarios suites", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The nine broker suites - s3, mqtt, kafka, amqp, nats, redis-streams, grpc, k8s, email - add a scenarios/ directory that the runner imports before calling runScenarios()."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_shared_persistence_contract", "label": "Shared persistence contract", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The eight persistence suites have no scenarios/ directory: they supply makeJournal / makeSnapshotStore / makeDurableStateStore and run sqlPersistenceScenarios(), whose cases live in lib/persistence-contract/ and are shared with the fast bun test pass (#390). A backend earns live coverage by writing a harness rather than another copy of the tests, and a case added for one backend is immediately checked against all of them."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_pg_wire_certification", "label": "Postgres-wire certification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "cockroachdb and yugabytedb are thinner still: they hand a description and a port to runPgWireSuite(), which drives the unmodified Postgres stores against the other server - certifying the wire-compatibility claim rather than asserting it (#401)."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_integration_compose_discovery", "label": "scripts/integration-compose.mjs suite discovery", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There used to be a package.json script per suite - 34 of them, the same two docker compose invocations with a different path - so the backend set was maintained in four places and missing one meant a suite that silently never ran (#559). A suite is now just a directory holding docker-compose.<dir>.yml; a wrong name prints the ones that exist. up stops at the first failing suite, teardown deliberately does not so one broken suite cannot strand later suites' containers and volumes."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_container_readiness_race", "label": "Container-started-but-broker-not-ready race", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single most common source of flake in these suites; every scenario guards against it with waitForPort(host, port)."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_why_not_testcontainers", "label": "Why not testcontainers/node", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bun compatibility is best-effort (the library expects Node's child_process event ordering); the stated requirement was locally runnable like tests/integration and compose YAML is the universal shape every developer already has muscle memory for; the compose files are ~20 lines each, so the abstraction cost outweighs the boilerplate saved."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_integration_brokers_workflow", "label": "integration-brokers.yml CI matrix", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs the broker suites as a job matrix; skipped on PRs touching only docs or unit tests via the same paths filter as integration.yml."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_adding_a_new_broker_suite", "label": "Adding a new broker suite", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prefer an image with a tini-style PID 1 so it exits cleanly on docker compose down instead of leaking zombies; create the three files; add an npm script (stale - the discovery script replaced them); optionally extend the CI matrix; guard readiness with waitForPort."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_per_suite_container_lifecycle", "label": "Per-suite container lifecycle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One broker container per suite rather than per test; fine for the current scenario count, revisitable if each it() should ever get a fresh broker."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_lib_waitforport_waitforport", "label": "waitForPort", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TCP/HTTP readiness probe in lib/WaitForPort.ts - the outside-in readiness gate for images compose cannot probe from within."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_lib_scenario_runscenarios", "label": "runScenarios", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_lib_persistencecontract_sqlpersistencescenarios", "label": "sqlPersistenceScenarios", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_lib_pgwirerunner_runpgwiresuite", "label": "runPgWireSuite", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_io_broker_kafkaactor_kafkaactor", "label": "KafkaActor", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_io_broker_amqpactor_amqpactor", "label": "AmqpActor", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_io_broker_natsactor_natsactor", "label": "NatsActor", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_io_broker_redisstreamsactor_redisstreamsactor", "label": "RedisStreamsActor", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_persistence_journals_postgresjournal_postgresjournal", "label": "PostgresJournal", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_persistence_journals_mariadbjournal_mariadbjournal", "label": "MariaDbJournal", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_persistence_journals_libsqljournal_libsqljournal", "label": "LibSqlJournal", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_persistence_journals_mssqljournal_mssqljournal", "label": "MsSqlJournal", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_persistence_journals_dynamodbjournal_dynamodbjournal", "label": "DynamoDbJournal", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_protocol_level_corners", "target": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_broker_live_integration_suites", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_auth_connection_bring_up", "target": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_broker_live_integration_suites", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/READM